  <!-- PRO promo banner: space reservation + early script fetch, moved here=
 from
       the end of <body> (see the "Banner script" block further down, which=
 still
       owns the ResizeObserver that tells Monaco to re-layout on resize -- =
that
       part needs #root, defined later in <body>, so it can't move here too=
).

       Vendor-reported: the header ad slot visibly overlaps this banner and=
 fills
       ~20% as a result -- confirmed via a live screenshot, and per direct
       investigation: "usually after rendering completely the position is
       correct but... initially renders on top of the ad/nav." Two real,
       file-verifiable causes, both fixed by moving here:

       1. This reservation rule previously lived in a <style> block at the =
very
          end of <body>, alongside the banner script. A CSS rule doesn't ap=
ply
          until the browser's parser reaches it -- so on initial layout, be=
fore
          the parser got that far, .header/.compiler-header-ad rendered wit=
h NO
          reservation at all, right at the top, only shifting down once the
          browser reached the old late <style> tag and reflowed. That's a
          timing-dependent, banner.js-independent bug: the reservation itse=
lf
          wasn't actually active at first paint despite reading as uncondit=
ional
          CSS. Declaring it here, in <head>, means it applies from the very
          first layout pass, before .header is ever laid out at all.
       2. banner.js itself was a plain <script src> with no async at the ve=
ry
          end of <body> -- the actual #pgz-banner element didn't exist unti=
l the
          browser finished parsing the entire rest of the page, which could=
 be
          well after the ad system's own (now-early, see runWhenReady in th=
e ad
          script below) request/render cycle. Fetching it here starts the
          download immediately without blocking parsing.

       Gated on $showPromoBanner (config.php/inc/campaign-schedule.php) sam=
e as
       the rest of this block -- see that file's doc comment for what's gat=
ed
       where and why. The fetch-then-inject pattern (rather than a plain
       <script src>) is the same client-side format-validation from banner.=
js's
       original location: only trust and execute banner.js if its cutoff da=
te
       is still expressed the way we expect. -->
